<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<!--
  S10 camera ring for the ANTBot + OpenArm build.

  Replaces antbot_description's S10CameraRing.

  DATUM: this package puts base_link ON the ground (see semi_humanoid_v2.urdf.xacro),
  while antbot_description puts it 17 mm below. Every z here is therefore the
  shared value minus 0.017, and the shared s10_front_xyz / s10_back_xyz strings
  can no longer be used verbatim - front and back are spelled out below with
  the same x/y and z = 0.350 - 0.017 = 0.333. If the upstream x/y ever move,
  these two lines must be updated by hand.

  The FRONT pitch still comes from antbot_description (s10_front_pitch, 30 deg).
  The BACK pitch is overridden here to 30 deg as well, against the shared
  15 deg - see s10_back_pitch_openarm below.

  The side units are moved off the stock ANTBot rack post onto the cargo box:
  (0.000, +-0.350, 0.550) instead of the shared (-0.100, +-0.320, 0.633), and
  pitched 40 deg instead of the shared 35 deg.

  Raising them to 0.550 and tilting to 40 deg keeps the near ground essentially
  where a 0.330 m / 30 deg mount put it - 0.161 m beyond the mount, 0.511 m
  from the robot centre - while restoring 0.205 m of near-clip margin: the
  lower-edge ground hit is at a 0.573 m slant against the 0.3 m clip plane
  (273 mm of margin, against 68 mm at 0.330 m / 30 deg).

  The cost is the upper edge: at 40 deg it sits 6.3 deg BELOW horizontal, so
  the side units see NOTHING at or above their own 0.550 m mount height, at
  any distance. Front and back, at 30 deg, look 3.7 deg up and have no such
  ceiling. Anything tall beside the robot - a person, a shelf, a stacked load -
  is absent from the side clouds. That is a deliberate trade: near-clip margin
  and near ground, bought with the side ceiling.

  The mount is the cargo box's FRONT CORNER POST (x -0.020..0.000,
  |y| 0.240..0.260, z 0.316..0.766): each unit sits beside that post at
  mid-height, 90 mm outboard of it and 9 mm above the box's own mid-height
  (0.541). A ~90 mm bracket off the post reaches it. The bracket is still not
  modelled.

  This placement clears the two conflicts the earlier (0.100, +-0.370, 0.913)
  mount had: it is 0.315 m below openarm_top_crossbar_link instead of buried in
  it, and with the lift up (shoulders at z = 0.815) link2 sits 0.169 m above
  the housing. With the lift DOWN (shoulders at z = 0.475) it is tight in both
  axes: link2 at zero joint angles occupies x 0.052..0.135, z 0.409..0.524, so
  the housing clears it by only 12 mm in x and 12 mm in z. openarm_*_joint1
  (axis Y) can swing the arm back through x = 0 on the way down. Keep the
  cameras in the planning scene rather than relying on nominal clearance.

  The stock ANTBot rack post the shared mounts were sized against does not
  exist here.

  Requires antbot_description/urdf/sensors.xacro to be included first - it
  provides the MrdvsS10 macro and the shared s10_* properties.
-->
<robot xmlns:xacro="http://ros.org/wiki/xacro">
  <!-- Side mounts on the cargo box. base_link is ON the ground, so z IS
       height above ground. Shared values for reference, re-datumed:
       x = -0.100, y = +-0.320, z = 0.633, pitch 35 deg. -->
  <!-- Back pitch, overridden. The shared ring uses 15 deg, which aims the rear
       unit mostly at the horizon; 30 deg matches the front unit, so front and
       back have identical coverage (same 0.333 height, same tilt): ground from
       0.165 m behind the mount instead of 0.293 m, upper edge 3.7 deg above
       horizontal instead of 18.7 deg. It also lifts the housing clear of
       base_chassis.stl, which the 15 deg mount grazed by ~1 mm. -->
  <xacro:property name="s10_back_pitch_openarm" value="${radians(30)}"/>

  <xacro:property name="s10_side_x_openarm" value="0.000"/>
  <xacro:property name="s10_side_y_openarm" value="0.350"/>
  <xacro:property name="s10_side_z_openarm" value="0.550"/>
  <xacro:property name="s10_side_pitch_openarm" value="${radians(40)}"/>

  <xacro:macro name="S10CameraRingOpenarm">
    <!-- x/y as antbot_description (0.380 / -0.390, y = 0); z re-datumed from
         the shared 0.350. Front pitch is upstream's; back pitch is overridden. -->
    <xacro:MrdvsS10 name="camera_s10_front"
      default_xyz="0.380 0.0 0.333" default_rpy="0.0 ${s10_front_pitch} 0.0"
      calibration_key="camera_s10_front_extrinsic"/>

    <xacro:MrdvsS10 name="camera_s10_back"
      default_xyz="-0.390 0.0 0.333" default_rpy="0.0 ${s10_back_pitch_openarm} ${radians(180)}"
      calibration_key="camera_s10_back_extrinsic"/>

    <!-- Overridden: on the cargo box front posts, 10 deg steeper than front/back. -->
    <xacro:MrdvsS10 name="camera_s10_left"
      default_xyz="${s10_side_x_openarm} ${s10_side_y_openarm} ${s10_side_z_openarm}"
      default_rpy="0.0 ${s10_side_pitch_openarm} ${radians(90)}"
      calibration_key="camera_s10_left_extrinsic"/>

    <xacro:MrdvsS10 name="camera_s10_right"
      default_xyz="${s10_side_x_openarm} ${-s10_side_y_openarm} ${s10_side_z_openarm}"
      default_rpy="0.0 ${s10_side_pitch_openarm} ${radians(-90)}"
      calibration_key="camera_s10_right_extrinsic"/>
  </xacro:macro>
</robot>
